","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/install-command#see-also","content":"Manifest System - Understanding skill-project.toml"},"892":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"page","content":"managed Command","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command"},"893":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command","content":"Keep this user's agent skills in line with a signed managed state using fastskill managed."},"894":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#managed-command","content":"managed Command"},"895":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#usage","content":"Usage"},"896":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"Settings"},"897":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#subcommands","content":"Subcommands"},"898":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#enroll","content":"enroll"},"899":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#apply","content":"apply"},"900":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#status","content":"status"},"901":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#unenroll","content":"unenroll"},"902":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Installs and other commands"},"903":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#the-quarantine","content":"The quarantine"},"904":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#managed-command","content":"Follow a **managed state**: a signed list of the skills one user's agents on this machine\nshould have, decided somewhere else. FastSkill checks its signature against keys pinned in\ntrusted settings, then deploys the listed skills into each agent's user skills folder, removes\nthe ones it put there that are no longer listed, and moves blocked content into a quarantine\ninstead of deleting it."},"905":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#managed-command","content":"Only FastSkill's own entries are changed. A skill folder that FastSkill didn't place and that\nholds other content than the state lists is reported as a collision and left alone."},"906":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"The source and the signing keys come only from two files, never from a project:"},"907":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"the system file, deployed by device management: `/etc/fastskill/managed.toml` (Linux),\n`/Library/Application Support/FastSkill/managed.toml` (macOS) or\n`%ProgramData%\\FastSkill\\managed.toml` (Windows). It must be owned by the administrator and\nwritable by nobody else;"},"908":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"the user file, `managed.toml` in FastSkill's configuration folder."},"909":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"A value in the system file wins over the same value in the user file."},"910":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#settings","content":"This release reads the state from a local file. The skill archives it lists are read from paths\nnext to it."},"911":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#enroll","content":"Enroll this user with the configured source and apply its first state. Enrolling again with the\nsame source keeps the machine id."},"912":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#apply","content":"Apply the newest signed state. When the system file names the source, the first apply enrolls\nthis user. Without network access to the source, the last accepted state is used and the report\nsays so. An expired state adds, changes and removes nothing, but blocked content is still\nquarantined."},"913":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#apply","content":"Only one apply runs at a time for a user. A second apply started from a terminal says so; one\nstarted without a terminal, such as from an agent hook, exits quietly. An apply that couldn't\ncomplete every step exits with an error after its report."},"914":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#status","content":"Show the source, the machine id, the state's subject and expiry, the last apply's targets and\ncollisions, and the quarantine. Nothing is changed."},"915":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#unenroll","content":"Remove what managed state put on this machine for this user: the skills FastSkill deployed (a\ndeployed copy that was changed is quarantined instead), the stored skills, the cached state,\nthe records and the user settings file. The quarantine is kept. Refused when the system file\nsets `required = true`, and while an apply runs."},"916":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#unenroll","content":"**Options** (every subcommand):"},"917":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#unenroll","content":"`--json`: Print the result as JSON"},"918":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-25","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"While this user follows a state, every command that adds or replaces skill content checks it\nfirst, before anything changes: `skill add`, `skill update`, `bundle add`, `bundle update`,\n`bundle override` (and resetting one), `project install` and restoring personal overrides. The\nsame check applies to `server serve` and `mcp serve`. Content whose digest is blocked is\nrefused, and when the state allows only the listed skills, so is anything it doesn't list. An\neditable local skill changes with every edit, so it skips the list, but never the block."},"919":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-26","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Other commands that read or change skills follow the state too:"},"920":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-27","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Situation"},"921":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-28","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"`managed`, `cache`, `repo`, `cli`"},"922":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-29","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Commands that read skills"},"923":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-30","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Commands that change content"},"924":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-31","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"Expired state"},"925":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-32","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run"},"926":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-33","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run, with a warning"},"927":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-34","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"refused"},"928":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-35","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"No valid state, `required = true`"},"929":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-36","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run"},"930":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-37","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"refused"},"931":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-38","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"refused"},"932":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-39","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"No valid state, not required"},"933":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-40","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run"},"934":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-41","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run, with a warning"},"935":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-42","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"run, with a warning"},"936":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-43","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#installs-and-other-commands","content":"`skill list` reports installed content the state blocks as `managed-blocked`, and content it\ndoesn't allow as `managed-not-allowed`; `skill list --check` fails on both. See\nreconciliation."},"937":{"id":"/cli-reference/managed-command-44","page_id":"/cli-reference/managed-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/managed-command#the-quarantine","content":"Content is moved, not deleted, when its digest is blocked, when the state allows only the\nlisted skills and claims the agent folders exclusively, or when a copy FastSkill deployed was\nchanged and is no longer listed. Each item keeps its former location, its digest and the\nreason, and `fastskill managed status` lists them."},"938":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","type":"page","content":"optimization commands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Quality"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command"},"939":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","content":"Run, resume, inspect, and export text-gradient skill optimization runs."},"940":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command#overview","content":"Overview"},"941":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command#usage","content":"Usage"},"942":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command#optimization-run","content":"optimization run"},"943":{"id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/optimize-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/optimize-command#optimization-resume","content":"optimization resum