enticated request."},"1521":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-196","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"When the token is short-lived, a program can print it: an identity provider CLI, or a\nscript that performs a CI job's token exchange. A credential command can only be\nsaved to your user `repositories.toml`, so `--auth-type command` requires `--user`.\nA `skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused."},"1522":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-197","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"The program runs directly, without a shell, from FastSkill's configuration\ndirectory, and is stopped after 30 seconds."},"1523":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-198","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"The first line of its standard output is the token. More than 16 KiB of output, an\nempty token, or a non-zero exit fails the request. Errors name the program and its\nexit status, never the token."},"1524":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-199","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"Standard error reaches your terminal only when there is one. When standard input\nor standard error is not a terminal, FastSkill sets `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0`, and\nthe command must print a token without prompting or exit non-zero."},"1525":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-200","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"It runs at most once per FastSkill process for each repository, and the token is\nkept in memory only."},"1526":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-201","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"With `bearer` and `command`, the token is sent only to the origin of the registry's\nindex URL. Downloads on other origins get no token, a redirect to another origin\ndrops it, and a redirect from `https` to `http` is refused. `repo list` and `repo info`\nshow the auth type, never the token."},"1527":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-202","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#credential-command","content":"Git sources use system Git credentials. A project manifest may use `pat` or `bearer`\nfor HTTP catalogs. See sources."},"1528":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-203","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"FastSkill supports multiple sources with priority-based resolution:"},"1529":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-204","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"**Resolution process**:"},"1530":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-205","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Repositories are consulted in ascending priority order (0 before 1 before 2)."},"1531":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-206","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"The first repository that satisfies the lookup wins for that skill id."},"1532":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-207","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Lower numeric priority means earlier in that order (0 is tried before 10)."},"1533":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-208","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"**Example**:"},"1534":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-209","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"`public-registry` (priority 0): `pptx v1.0.0`"},"1535":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-210","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"`team-skills` (priority 1): `pptx v1.2.0`"},"1536":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-211","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#multi-source-skill-resolution","content":"Result: `pptx v1.0.0` from `public-registry` is used because priority 0 is consulted first."},"1537":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-212","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#creating-a-git-marketplace","content":"`--owner-name` is required: Claude Code rejects a marketplace without an\nowner. Run `claude plugin validate .` to check the generated file against\nClaude Code's own rules."},"1538":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-213","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."},"1539":{"id":"/cli-reference/repository-command-214","page_id":"/cli-reference/repository-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repository-command#troubleshooting","content":"**Verify cre