-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#summarize-the-run","content":"Summarize the run"},"2151":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-4","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#re-score-without-re-running-agent","content":"Re-score without re-running agent"},"2152":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-5","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#ci-usage-pattern","content":"CI usage pattern"},"2153":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-6","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Practical gating policy"},"2154":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-7","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"See also"},"2155":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-8","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"This workflow is the day-to-day path for quality checks. If you haven't authored a suite yet — the `[tool.fastskill.eval]` table, prompts CSV, and checks TOML — start with Eval setup first; pass/fail behavior (especially the inert `should_trigger` column, choosing between `skill_invoked` and `trigger_expectation`, and what `required = false` does) is documented there."},"2156":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-9","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"`--output-dir` is required on every `eval run` invocation — there is no default output location. All examples below include it. Each run lands under `<output-dir>/<timestamp>/<agent>/` (a numeric suffix is appended if that timestamp directory already exists) — that per-agent directory, not `<output-dir>` itself, is what `--run-dir` expects below."},"2157":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-10","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"**Runs are isolated by default.** Each case executes in a per-case scratch workspace containing only the skill under test (`SKILL.md` beside `skill-project.toml`, named by `[metadata].id`), with user-level skill discovery suppressed where the backend supports it. The `isolation:` line in the output (and the `isolation` object in `summary.json`) reports what each run actually got; a failed case's workspace survives under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to run in the project root against your machine's ambient environment — and expect trigger rates measured before isolation existed to re-baseline on the first isolated run."},"2158":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-11","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"Common focused runs:"},"2159":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-12","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#summarize-the-run","content":"Use this for release notes and quick stakeholder review."},"2160":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-13","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#re-score-without-re-running-agent","content":"Use this when scoring logic changed and you want consistency across previous runs."},"2161":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-14","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block merge if smoke tag fails"},"2162":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-15","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block release if full suite fails"},"2163":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-16","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Keep per-tag pass-rate trends to detect slow quality drift"},"2164":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-17","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Eval setup"},"2165":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-18","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2166":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-19","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2167":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"page","content":"Eval Setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Evaluate and optimize","Evaluations"],"tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup"},"2168":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-0","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup","content":"Author an eval suite: the [tool.fastskill.eval] manifest table, the prompts CSV, and the checks TOML schema."},"2169":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-1","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#eval-setup","content":"Eval Setup"},"2170":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-2","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"2171":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-3","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"1\\. The `[tool.fastskill.eval]` table"},"2172":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-4","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Validate the config"},"2173":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-5","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"2\\. The prompts CSV"},"2174":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-6","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"3\\. Checks: `checks.toml` (optional)"},"2175":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-7","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill_invoked`"},"2176":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-8","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`trigger_expectation`"},"2177":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-9","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`command_contains`"},"2178":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-10","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`file_exists`"},"2179":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-11","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`max_tool_calls` (alias: `max_command_count`)"},"2180":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-12","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Making a check advisory with `required`"},"2181":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-13","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"How a case's pass/fail is decided"},"2182":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-14","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"4\\. Validate, then run, then report"},"2183":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-15","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Setup checklist"},"2184":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-16","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"See also"},"2185":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-17","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#eval-setup","content":"This page is the reference for **authoring** an eval suite: the config table in `skill-project.toml`, the prompts CSV a suite is made of, and the optional checks TOML that actually decides pass/fail. Work through it top to bottom once, then use Run evals for the day-to-day commands."},"2186":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-18","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#eval-setup","content":"For guided suite design, use the FastSkill skill.\nIts eval-authoring workflow\nand copyable invoice example are maintained and packaged in the skills repository."},"2187":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-19","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"`skill-project.toml` exists (project root or skill directory — `fastskill` walks up the tree to find it)."},"2188":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-20","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"`SKILL.md` exists alongside it if you're authoring a single skill's suite."},"2189":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-21","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"For `fastskill eval run`: a supported agent CLI on `PATH`. Agent keys come from aikit-sdk: `aikit`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, and `pi`. A key is accepted only when its CLI is detected on the current machine; a typo and an uninstalled agent both error with `RUNTIME_UNKNOWN_ID`. `fastskill eval validate --all` reports which keys are detected in *your* environment."},"2190":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-22","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"Deterministic validation and scoring need no model credential. Target execution needs the\nselected runtime's authentication; native judges separately need their configured endpoint,\nmodel, and credential environment variable. Embedding configuration is unrelated."},"2191":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-23","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Add this table to `skill-project.toml`. Every path is resolved relative to the **skill project root** (the directory containing `skill-project.toml`) unless it's absolute."},"2192":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-24","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Field"},"2193":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-25","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Type"},"2194":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-26","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Required"},"2195":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-27","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Default"},"2196":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-28","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Meaning"},"2197":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-29","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`prompts`"},"2198":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-30","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"path"},"2199":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-31","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**yes**"},"2200":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-32","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"—"},"2201":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-33","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Path to the prompts CSV."},"2202":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-34","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`checks`"},"2203":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-35","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"path"},"2204":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-36","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2205":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-37","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"none"},"2206":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-38","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Path to the checks TOML. Even when omitted, `should_trigger` produces a per-case trigger expectation — see the callout below."},"2207":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-39","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`timeout_seconds`"},"2208":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-40","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2209":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-41","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2210":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-42","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`900`"},"2211":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-43","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Per-case timeout passed to the agent run."},"2212":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-44","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`trials_per_case`"},"2213":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-45","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2214":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-46","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2215":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-47","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`1`"},"2216":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-48","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Trials run per case; validated to `[1, 1000]` (`EVAL_INVALID_TRIALS_CONFIG` otherwise)."},"2217":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-49","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`parallel`"},"2218":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-50","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2219":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-51","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2220":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-52","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"unset (CPU core count)"},"2221":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-53","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Max concurrent trials for one case."},"2222":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-54","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`pass_threshold`"},"2223":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-55","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"float"},"2224":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-56","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2225":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-57","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`1.0`"},"2226":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-58","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Fraction of trials that must pass for a case to be marked passed; validated to `[0.0, 1.0]` (`EVAL_INVALID_THRESHOLD` otherwise)."},"2227":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-59","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`fail_on_missing_agent`"},"2228":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-60","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"bool"},"2229":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-61","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2230":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-62","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**`true`**"},"2231":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-63","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"If true, `eval run` and `eval validate --agent <key>` error with `EVAL_AGENT_UNAVAILABLE` when the chosen agent isn't installed."},"2232":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-64","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."},"2233":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-65","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"With no `checks` file configured, each case still receives the required skill-consultation expectation implied by `should_trigger`. A successful process exit alone is not enough. Add a checks file for further deterministic outcome or adherence evidence."},"2234":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-66","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Real output against a working config (this one set `timeout_seconds = 120` and `fail_on_missing_agent = false`):"},"2235":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-67","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"},"2236":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-68","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"A prompts CSV missing a required column fails the same way:"},"2237":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-69","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."},"2238":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-70","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Column"},"2239":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-71","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Required"},"2240":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-72","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Meaning"},"2241":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-73","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`id`"},"2242":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-74","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2243":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-75","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Non-empty identifier per row. Used for `--case`, artifact folder names, and reports."},"2244":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-76","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`prompt`"},"2245":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-77","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2246":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-78","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Text sent to the agent. Use CSV quoting (`\"...\"`, doubled `\"\"` for an embedded quote) for commas or newlines."},"2247":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-79","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`should_trigger`"},"2248":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-80","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2249":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-81","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`true`/`1` (case-insensitive `true`) or anything else counts as `false`. It creates a required per-case skill-consultation expectation; see below."},"2250":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-82","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`tags`"},"2251":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-83","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2252":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-84","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Comma-separated tags inside the cell (e.g. `\"smoke,basic\"`). Used by `eval run --tag <name>`."},"2253":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-85","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`workspace_subdir`"},"2254":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-86","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2255":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-87","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Relative path that becomes the agent's working directory for the case. Under the default isolation it is created **inside the case's scratch workspace**, with fixture files copied in from the same path under the project root; under `--no-isolation` it resolves directly under the project root. Empty or omitted → workspace root."},"2256":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-88","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Empty lines are skipped."},"2257":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-89","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"**`should_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."},"2258":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-90","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"This is adherence/selection evidence, not outcome correctness. A structured `Skill` call is direct evidence; supported decoders may also recognize a tool input that references the staged skill-document path. The path proxy indicates consultation, not that the instructions were read or followed. Pair positive cases with outcome checks or judges."},"2259":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-91","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"Point `checks` at a TOML file with one or more `[[check]]` tables, keyed by the required `name` field. There are exactly five check types (`aikit_evals::checks::CheckDefinition`):"},"2260":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-92","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."},"2261":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-93","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"The check you almost certainly want for \"did my skill fire?\"."},"2262":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-94","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Field"},"2263":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-95","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Type"},"2264":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-96","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Required"},"2265":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-97","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Default"},"2266":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-98","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill`"},"2267":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-99","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string"},"2268":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-100","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2269":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-101","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"— (omit to match *any* skill invocation)"},"2270":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-102","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`expected`"},"2271":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-103","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2272":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-104","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2273":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-105","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true` (`false` asserts the skill did **not** run)"},"2274":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-106","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`required`"},"2275":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-107","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2276":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-108","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2277":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-109","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true`"},"2278":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-110","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`cases`"},"2279":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-111","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string array"},"2280":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-112","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2281":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-113","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"all cases (exact case IDs)"},"2282":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-114","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Matches a structured `Skill` invocation or, where the decoder supplies it, a tool input referring to the staged skill-document path. When `skill` is given, a structured invocation must exactly match its identifying field. A skill name merely mentioned in unrelated prose does not count. Path-reference matching improves portability but remains a consultation proxy rather than proof of adherence."},"2283":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-115","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Every check type supports `cases = [\"case-id\", ...]`, selecting exact case IDs. An absent selector applies to every case. Use selectors for checks that should not run across a mixed suite."},"2284":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-116","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Field"},"2285":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-117","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Type"},"2286":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-118","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Required"},"2287":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-119","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Default"},"2288":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-120","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`pattern`"},"2289":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-121","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"string"},"2290":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-122","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2291":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-123","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"—"},"2292":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-124","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`expected`"},"2293":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-125","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2294":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-126","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2295":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-127","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"— (`true` = pattern must appear, `false` = must NOT appear)"},"2296":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-128","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`required`"},"2297":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-129","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2298":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-130","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"no"},"2299":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-131","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`true`"},"2300":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-132","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Matches `pattern` as a **plain substring** against the JSONL trace. Prefer `skill_invoked` for asserting that a skill ran; treat `trigger_expectation` as the escape hatch for matching arbitrary text the agent produced."},"2301":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-133","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Field"},"2302":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-134","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Type"},"2303":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-135","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Required"},"2304":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-136","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Default"},"2305":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-137","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`pattern`"},"2306":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-138","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"string"},"2307":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-139","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"yes"},"2308":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-140","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"—"},"2309":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-141","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`required`"},"2310":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-142","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"bool"},"2311":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-143","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"no"},"2312":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-144","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`true`"},"2313":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-145","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Same trace substring search as `trigger_expectation`, without the pass/fail inversion — passes if the pattern is found anywhere in the trace."},"2314":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-146","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Field"},"2315":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-147","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Type"},"2316":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-148","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Required"},"2317":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-149","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Default"},"2318":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-150","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`path`"},"2319":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-151","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"path"},"2320":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-152","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"yes"},"2321":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-153","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"—"},"2322":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-154","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`required`"},"2323":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-155","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"bool"},"2324":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-156","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"no"},"2325":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-157","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`true`"},"2326":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-158","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Passes if `path` exists under the case's working directory — the case's scratch workspace under the default isolation (plus `workspace_subdir` when set), or the project root under `--no-isolation`."},"2327":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-159","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Field"},"2328":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-160","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Type"},"2329":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-161","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Required"},"2330":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-162","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Default"},"2331":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-163","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`limit`"},"2332":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-164","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"integer"},"2333":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-165","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"yes"},"2334":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-166","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"—"},"2335":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-167","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`required`"},"2336":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-168","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"bool"},"2337":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-169","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"no"},"2338":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-170","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`true`"},"2339":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-171","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Passes if the number of **tool invocations** the agent made is `<= limit`."},"2340":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-172","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"A tool invocation is a structured `tool_use` trace event, plus any `raw_json` trace line — the\nlatter covers backends that still emit tool calls as raw JSON instead of decoded tool events.\nAssistant text output, token-usage events, and unmodelled SDK event variants are **not** counted."},"2341":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-173","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Results use `\"check_name\": \"max_tool_calls\"`. The per-case artifact field counting\nthese events is `command_count`."},"2342":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-174","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Every check type accepts `required` (default `true`). Setting `required = false` makes the check **advisory**: it still runs, and its result still appears in the run artifacts with its own `passed` value, but a failure does not fail the case."},"2343":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-175","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Use it for signal you want visible in reports without gating the suite on it."},"2344":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-176","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"No `checks` file configured (or it loads zero explicit checks): the case still receives the required trigger expectation generated from `should_trigger`."},"2345":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-177","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Any checks loaded: the case **passes** only if every **required** check's `passed` is `true`. Checks marked `required = false` are reported but never fail the case. Among required checks there is no partial credit and no threshold — they are all-or-nothing per case."},"2346":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-178","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."},"2347":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-179","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A trial that times out is always `error`, independent of checks."},"2348":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-180","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Across trials, `pass_threshold` decides the case's aggregated status: pass rate across trials must be `>= pass_threshold`."},"2349":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-181","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"Once the manifest, CSV, and checks file exist:"},"2350":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-182","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--output-dir` is **required** on `fastskill eval run` — there is no default. Omitting it fails argument parsing before anything else runs:"},"2351":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-183","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive on both `eval run` and `eval validate` — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` additionally requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`); on `eval validate` both are optional — omit them to validate config without checking any agent's availability."},"2352":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-184","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"See Run evals for the full day-to-day command set, artifact layout, and CI gating pattern."},"2353":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-185","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`[tool.fastskill.eval]` present with a `prompts` path that resolves."},"2354":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-186","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Prompts CSV has `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger` headers (plus `tags` / `workspace_subdir` if you use them)."},"2355":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-187","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Each `should_trigger` value reflects the required consultation/non-consultation expectation; explicit `skill_invoked` checks do not contradict it."},"2356":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-188","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Outcome correctness is measured separately where consultation alone is insufficient."},"2357":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-189","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`fastskill eval validate --all` passes and lists the agent you intend to run against as available."},"2358":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-190","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Output directory convention agreed for `--output-dir` (local + CI)."},"2359":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-191","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Run evals"},"2360":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-192","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2361":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-193","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2362":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"page","content":"Advanced Patterns","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Workflow examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns"},"2363":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-0","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns","content":"Analyze overlap, optimize skills, filter project groups, and manage editable and global skills."},"2364":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-1","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#overview","content":"Overview"},"2365":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-2","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Find duplicate and overlapping skills"},"2366":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-3","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#improve-a-skill-with-optimization","content":"Improve a skill with `optimization`"},"2367":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-4","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#install-only-part-of-a-collection-with-groups","content":"Install only part of a collection with groups"},"2368":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-5","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"Editable and recursive local skills"},"2369":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-6","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Project vs. global scope"},"2370":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-7","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#overview","content":"These are real, source-backed workflows for teams managing many skills. Every command below exists in\nthe CLI."},"2371":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-8","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"As a collection grows, skills drift into overlap. `fastskill analysis` surfaces that:"},"2372":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-9","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`analysis duplicates` supports filtering and output control:"},"2373":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-10","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Flag"},"2374":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-11","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Purpose"},"2375":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-12","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--threshold`"},"2376":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-13","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Minimum similarity to report"},"2377":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-14","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--limit`"},"2378":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-15","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Maximum number of pairs to show"},"2379":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-16","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--severity`"},"2380":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-17","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Filter by minimum severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `all`"},"2381":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-18","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--format`"},"2382":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-19","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`table`, `json`, `grid`, or `xml` (`--json` is shorthand)"},"2383":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-20","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#improve-a-skill-with-optimization","content":"`fastskill optimization` runs a text-gradient loop to iteratively improve a skill's content:"},"2384":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-21","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#install-only-part-of-a-collection-with-groups","content":"Skills can be tagged into groups; installs can include or exclude them (poetry-style):"},"2385":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-22","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"For local skill development, add without copying and add whole trees at once:"},"2386":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-23","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"After editing an editable skill in place, run `fastskill index rebuild` so semantic search and resolve\nreflect the changes."},"2387":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-24","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Most commands default to the current project. Use `--global` to operate on the shared user-level\nskills directory (`~/.config/fastskill/skills`, tracked by `global-skills.lock`):"},"2388":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-25","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Use `analysis` to keep a collection tidy, `optimization` to sharpen individual skills, and group\nfilters\nplus `--global` to control what gets installed where."},"2389":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"page","content":"Integration Tutorials","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Workflow examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials"},"2390":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-0","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials","content":"Connect FastSkill to agents and pipelines: MCP into Claude Code and Cursor, the serve HTTP API, and locked installs in CI."},"2391":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-1","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#overview","content":"Overview"},"2392":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-2","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"1\\. MCP into Claude Code"},"2393":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-3","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"2\\. MCP into Cursor"},"2394":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-4","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"3\\. Call the HTTP API from an app"},"2395":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-5","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"4\\. Reproducible installs in CI"},"2396":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-6","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#overview","content":"These tutorials cover FastSkill's real integration surfaces: the **MCP** server for agents, the\n**HTTP API** from `fastskill server serve`, and **locked installs** in CI. Each uses commands and endpoints\nthat exist in the tool."},"2397":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-7","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"Expose FastSkill to Claude Code as MCP tools — read-only unless you start the server with\n`--enable-write`."},"2398":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-8","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"Claude Code will now see tools named after complete command paths, such as\n`fastskill_skill_search`, `fastskill_skill_list`, `fastskill_skill_read`, and\n`fastskill_repo_show`. Mutating tools such as `fastskill_project_install` and\n`fastskill_repo_add` are withheld until the server is started with `--enable-write`; see\nWrite access. To point the agent at a running HTTP MCP\nserver instead of spawning FastSkill itself:"},"2399":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-9","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"Same flow, different agent key:"},"2400":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-10","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"Supported agents: `claude`, `cursor`, `gemini`, `copilot`, `opencode`, `codex`. See the full\nMCP tool-calling guide."},"2401":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-11","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"Run the server and use the versioned `/api/v1/...` REST surface. Start read-only:"},"2402":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-12","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"These are all read endpoints and work without `--enable-write`. To manage skills over HTTP (install /\nupdate / delete), start with `fastskill server serve --enable-write`, and front the port with an\nauthenticating proxy if it is exposed — `server serve` enforces no auth of its own. See the\n`server serve` reference and security model."},"2403":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-13","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`, then install exact locked versions in the pipeline:"},"2404":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-14","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` from a CI secret if the pipeline needs semantic search or reindex; without it\nthose steps skip silently rather than failing."},"2405":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-15","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"For agents, install FastSkill as an MCP server. For services and pipelines, use the `server serve`\nHTTP API and `project install --lock`. There is no separate SDK to integrate — the CLI, MCP tools,\nand HTTP API are the surface."},"2406":{"id":"/integration/agents","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"page","content":"Documentation and tools for agents","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents"},"2407":{"id":"/integration/agents-0","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents","content":"Retrieve current FastSkill documentation as Markdown and use the CLI or MCP safely."},"2408":{"id":"/integration/agents-1","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"Read the documentation"},"2409":{"id":"/integration/agents-2","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Inspect the CLI contract"},"2410":{"id":"/integration/agents-3","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Preview, apply, verify"},"2411":{"id":"/integration/agents-4","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Agent skills and MCP"},"2412":{"id":"/integration/agents-5","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"This site documents one release. The release number appears on every page and in\nall Markdown exports. Start with llms.txt, follow its per-page Markdown\nlinks, or download llms-full.txt. These URLs need no authentication\nor browser JavaScript. Each page also provides View Markdown and Copy Markdown."},"2413":{"id":"/integration/agents-6","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Match the binary version to the documentation. `cli spec` describes the installed\nbinary's complete command tree and flags. Use only the flags supported by that\ncommand; `--json` is not a global flag."},"2414":{"id":"/integration/agents-7","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Check the process exit status and the returned diagnostics. A valid JSON response\ncan describe failure or partial success. Dry runs validate a plan without changing\nmanaged state; online plans can still fetch inputs. Use `--offline` when supported\nand when required verified content is already available locally."},"2415":{"id":"/integration/agents-8","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Installed skills provide task instructions. FastSkill's MCP tools provide package\noperations. They are separate interfaces; reading a skill does not require an MCP\nserver. See Claude Code and\nCursor for installation locations and registration."},"2416":{"id":"/integration/agents-9","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"The server exposes read-only tools by default. Mutating tools require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`. Tool names use the full command path, for example\n`fastskill_skill_read` and `fastskill_project_install`. See\nMCP tool access for write configuration."},"2417":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"page","content":"Claude Code Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration"},"2418":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Claude Code for intelligent skill discovery."},"2419":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Overview"},"2420":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-2","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"2421":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-3","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"2422":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-4","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"GitHub Actions"},"2423":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-5","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2424":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-6","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"MCP Registration"},"2425":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-7","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"HTTP API"},"2426":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-8","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Claude Code reads skills **directly** from the skills directory (`.claude/skills/` by\ndefault). FastSkill's job is to get the right skills onto disk and keep them reconciled with\nyour manifest — once a skill is installed, Claude Code discovers it natively. There is no\nmetadata file to generate or keep in sync."},"2427":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-9","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"That's it — the next time Claude Code runs in this project, the installed skills are available."},"2428":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-10","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"`fastskill project install` / `fastskill skill add` materializes skills into the configured\n`skills_directory` (default `.claude/skills/`)."},"2429":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-11","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Each skill is a folder containing `SKILL.md` plus its resources."},"2430":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-12","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Claude Code scans that directory and loads skills by their `SKILL.md` frontmatter — no\nexport or sync step is involved."},"2431":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-13","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` to see exactly what an agent loads, or\n`fastskill skill read <skill-id> --meta` for just the metadata."},"2432":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-14","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"Keep the skills directory reconciled in CI so commits always carry the resolved skill set:"},"2433":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-15","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."},"2434":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-16","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Wrong skills directory:** Claude Code and FastSkill must agree on the location. The default\nis `.claude/skills/`; override it via `skills_directory` under `[tool.fastskill]` in\n`skill-project.toml` or the `--skills-dir` flag."},"2435":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-17","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"Register `fastskill` as an MCP server inside Claude Code with a single command:"},"2436":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-18","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"After running the command, reload Claude Code. The tools exposed by\n`fastskill mcp serve --transport stdio` will be callable from the agent — the read-only ones only.\nMutating tools (`fastskill_project_install`, `fastskill_skill_add`,\n`fastskill_skill_remove`, …) require `mcp serve --enable-write`; see\nWrite access."},"2437":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-19","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"`fastskill server serve` exposes FastSkill's versioned application API under `/api/v1/…`, for example `GET /api/v1/status` and `GET /api/v1/skills`."},"2438":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-20","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"The old Claude-compatible `/v1/skills…` HTTP surface is no longer part of the public server. Use the MCP integration above for Claude Code and use `/api/v1/…` for HTTP clients."},"2439":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-21","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"See the agent’s skill documentation for native discovery behavior."},"2440":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"page","content":"Cursor Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration"},"2441":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Cursor IDE for intelligent skill discovery and tool recommendations."},"2442":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/c