,"page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"Scans for `SKILL.md` files"},"3152":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-122","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"Reads `skill-project.toml` if present (takes priority for all fields)"},"3153":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-123","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"Extracts metadata from `SKILL.md` YAML frontmatter as fallback"},"3154":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-124","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"Applies field-by-field priority: skill-project.toml > SKILL.md"},"3155":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-125","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"Generates the marketplace.json file in Claude Code format"},"3156":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-126","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#command-behavior","content":"**Note**: `skill-project.toml` provides metadata support (id, version, description, author, tags, capabilities, download\\_url). The `id` field is required and must not contain slashes. The `name` field is not used in skill-project.toml - skill names for display come from `SKILL.md` frontmatter only. All fields in skill-project.toml take priority over SKILL.md frontmatter."},"3157":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-127","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"When generating `marketplace.json`, all metadata fields follow this priority order:"},"3158":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-128","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"**skill-project.toml** `[metadata]` section (highest priority)"},"3159":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-129","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"Fields: `id` (required, no slashes), `version` (required), `description`, `author`, `tags`, `capabilities`, `download_url`"},"3160":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-130","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"All fields from skill-project.toml take precedence over SKILL.md"},"3161":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-131","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"The `id` field is required and must not contain slashes or scope information"},"3162":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-132","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"**SKILL.md** frontmatter (fallback)"},"3163":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-133","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"Used for: `name` (display only), `description`, `author`, `tags`, `capabilities`"},"3164":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-134","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"`name` in SKILL.md is for display purposes only, not for package identification"},"3165":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-135","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"This field-by-field priority allows skill authors to:"},"3166":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-136","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"Override specific fields in skill-project.toml while keeping others in SKILL.md"},"3167":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-137","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"Supplement SKILL.md metadata with additional fields in skill-project.toml"},"3168":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-138","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"Maintain version control separately from SKILL.md content"},"3169":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-139","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#metadata-priority","content":"**Example**: If skill-project.toml has `version = \"2.0.0\"` but SKILL.md has `version: \"1.0.0\"`, the marketplace.json will use `\"2.0.0\"`. Similarly, if skill-project.toml has `author = \"New Author\"`, it will override the author from SKILL.md. The `name` field always comes from SKILL.md frontmatter for display purposes, as it is not present in skill-project.toml."},"3170":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-140","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#validation","content":"The registry validates `marketplace.json` files:"},"3171":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-141","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#validation","content":"All required fields must be present"},"3172":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-142","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#validation","content":"`id`, `name`, and `description` must not be empty"},"3173":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-143","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#validation","content":"Skills with invalid data are skipped"},"3174":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-144","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#caching","content":"Marketplace.json files are cached for 5 minutes to reduce network requests. To force a refresh:"},"3175":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-145","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#caching","content":"Wait 5 minutes for cache expiry"},"3176":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-146","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#caching","content":"Restart the server"},"3177":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-147","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#caching","content":"Clear cache manually (future feature)"},"3178":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-148","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#best-practices","content":"**Keep it updated**: Regenerate `marketplace.json` when skills change"},"3179":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-149","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#best-practices","content":"**Use semantic versioning**: Use clear version identifiers"},"3180":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-150","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#best-practices","content":"**Include all metadata**: Provide tags, capabilities, and author information"},"3181":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-151","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#best-practices","content":"**Test accessibility**: Verify the URL is accessible from your environment"},"3182":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-152","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#best-practices","content":"**Version control**: Commit `marketplace.json` to your repository"},"3183":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-153","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#see-also","content":"Repository Command"},"3184":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-154","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#see-also","content":"Sources Configuration"},"3185":{"id":"/registry/marketplace-json-155","page_id":"/registry/marketplace-json","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/marketplace-json#see-also","content":"Registry Overview"},"3186":{"id":"/registry/overview","page_id":"/registry/overview","type":"page","content":"Sources and catalogs","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams","Sources and catalogs"],"tags":[],"url":"/registry/overview"},"3187":{"id":"/registry/overview-0","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview","content":"Discover skills from configured sources and choose how to distribute a team setup."},"3188":{"id":"/registry/overview-1","page_id":"/registry/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"Choose a source"},"3189":{"id":"/registry/overview-2","page_id":"/registry/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/overview#discover-and-install","content":"Discover and install"},"3190":{"id":"/registry/overview-3","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview","content":"A repository configuration gives FastSkill a named source for discovering and\ninstalling skills. It is separate from the installed skill directory and from the\nlocal browser console."},"3191":{"id":"/registry/overview-4","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."},"3192":{"id":"/registry/overview-5","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"**HTTP registry**: an HTTP index and downloadable skill artifacts."},"3193":{"id":"/registry/overview-6","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"**ZIP catalog**: a base URL exposing marketplace metadata and ZIP downloads."},"3194":{"id":"/registry/overview-7","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"**Local catalog**: skill content and catalog metadata on disk."},"3195":{"id":"/registry/overview-8","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#choose-a-source","content":"See source configuration for the manifest fields, authentication,\nand direct Git origins. For an exact portable team setup, use\nbundles."},"3196":{"id":"/registry/overview-9","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#discover-and-install","content":"The following commands assume a configured repository named `team`; replace the\nexample skill ID with a result from that repository:"},"3197":{"id":"/registry/overview-10","page_id":"/registry/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/overview#discover-and-install","content":"Search discovers candidates; installation records a selected origin and content.\nCommit the manifest and lock together so teammates can restore the intended state.\nSee repository commands for management actions\nand marketplace.json for catalog authoring."},"3198":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","type":"page","content":"Choose a distribution model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams","Sources and catalogs"],"tags":[],"url":"/registry/repository-architecture"},"3199":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-0","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Decide between direct sources, catalogs, and self-contained team bundles."},"3200":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-1","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/repository-architecture#discovery-and-installation","content":"Discovery and installation"},"3201":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-2","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/repository-architecture#team-reproducibility","content":"Team reproducibility"},"3202":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-3","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/repository-architecture#trust","content":"Trust"},"3203":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-4","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Need"},"3204":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-5","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Use"},"3205":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-6","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Iterate on one skill locally"},"3206":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-7","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"A local dependency, optionally editable"},"3207":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-8","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Install a skill from a source repository"},"3208":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-9","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"A Git origin with a branch or tag"},"3209":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-10","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Discover and select skills across a team"},"3210":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-11","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"A Git marketplace, local catalog, HTTP registry, or ZIP catalog"},"3211":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-12","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"Share an exact skill set without original source access"},"3212":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-13","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture","content":"A self-contained bundle"},"3213":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-14","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture#discovery-and-installation","content":"Catalog search returns metadata and an install reference. It does not install a\nskill. Adding a result records its origin and materializes the selected content.\nLocks record the resolved selection so restoration does not silently pick a newer\ncatalog version or Git commit."},"3214":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-15","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture#discovery-and-installation","content":"A project's manifest defines its repository configuration. Give each catalog a\nunique name and use explicit repository selection where IDs overlap. See\nconfiguration examples."},"3215":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-16","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture#team-reproducibility","content":"Commit the manifest and lock together. Preserve any local source files and bundled\nartifacts required for restoration. A fresh machine still needs network access for\nuncached remote dependencies; `--offline` cannot download missing content."},"3216":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-17","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture#team-reproducibility","content":"For an artifact recipients can install without access to private source repositories,\nbuild a bundle. Bundles retain ownership so removing\none package does not remove a skill that another package still requires."},"3217":{"id":"/registry/repository-architecture-18","page_id":"/registry/repository-architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/repository-architecture#trust","content":"A digest proves that selected content has not changed; it does not establish that\nthe instructions or scripts are safe. Review sources before making them available\nto agents. See the security model."},"3218":{"id":"/registry/sources","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"page","content":"Configure skill sources","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams","Sources and catalogs"],"tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources"},"3219":{"id":"/registry/sources-0","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources","content":"Add skills from Git and configure local, Git marketplace, HTTP, and ZIP catalogs."},"3220":{"id":"/registry/sources-1","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources#install-directly-from-git","content":"Install directly from Git"},"3221":{"id":"/registry/sources-2","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources#migrating-from-tree-urls","content":"Migrating from `/tree/` URLs"},"3222":{"id":"/registry/sources-3","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources#configure-a-catalog","content":"Configure a catalog"},"3223":{"id":"/registry/sources-4","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Registry authentication"},"3224":{"id":"/registry/sources-5","page_id":"/registry/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/sources#publish-a-catalog","content":"Publish a catalog"},"3225":{"id":"/registry/sources-6","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources","content":"Complete the quickstart first. Commands below use example URLs and\nIDs: replace them with a repository you can access and a skill it actually contains."},"3226":{"id":"/registry/sources-7","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#install-directly-from-git","content":"Use one ref selector for a source. For a skill in a subdirectory, declare the clean\nclone URL and `subdir` in the manifest, then install it:"},"3227":{"id":"/registry/sources-8","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#install-directly-from-git","content":"Use this manifest form as the portable source of truth for subdirectories. It keeps the clone URL,\nbranch, and subdirectory explicit in committed project state.\nFastSkill uses system Git; install Git and ensure it can access the repository before\nadding private sources. Git credentials come from your Git configuration."},"3228":{"id":"/registry/sources-9","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#migrating-from-tree-urls","content":"Manifests written by fastskill 0.9.221 and earlier recorded a GitHub browser link as the\ngit `url`, e.g., `https://github.com/your-org/skills/tree/main/review-notes`. Git cannot\nclone such a URL. Manifest `schema_version = \"2\"` splits it into the three fields shown\nabove, and fastskill performs that split while reading — no manual edit is needed. The\nrewritten form reaches disk the next time a command saves the manifest, e.g.,\n`skill add` or `skill remove` (`project install` reads it and updates only `skills.lock`). A `/tree/` URL in a manifest that\nalready declares `schema_version = \"2\"` is an error, and the message shows the corrected\nTOML."},"3229":{"id":"/registry/sources-10","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#migrating-from-tree-urls","content":"One consequence is worth planning for: a manifest saved by a current fastskill declares\n`schema_version = \"2\"`, and fastskill 0.9.232 and earlier refuse to read it. Upgrade every\nmachine and CI job that shares the project before the first save."},"3230":{"id":"/registry/sources-11","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#migrating-from-tree-urls","content":"The manifest records the requested origin/ref; the lock records the selected commit\nand integrity evidence. `project install --lock` restores that selection even when\na branch advances. `skill update` deliberately refreshes the origin. Repository\nversion/strategy controls do not apply to Git origins."},"3231":{"id":"/registry/sources-12","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#migrating-from-tree-urls","content":"Offline restoration needs the verified source content in the local cache. A lockfile\nalone does not contain the source files. Run an online install first, or distribute\nself-contained bundles."},"3232":{"id":"/registry/sources-13","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#configure-a-catalog","content":"A catalog lets you discover skills and add them by their canonical IDs. Each\nrepository is an entry in `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` in `skill-project.toml`.\nLower priority numbers are searched first. Explicit `--repository NAME` selection\navoids ambiguity when several catalogs offer the same ID."},"3233":{"id":"/registry/sources-14","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#configure-a-catalog","content":"Relative local repository paths are resolved from the directory containing\n`skill-project.toml`. They therefore keep the same meaning when FastSkill is invoked from a\nnested project directory."},"3234":{"id":"/registry/sources-15","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#configure-a-catalog","content":"`zip_url` is the manifest field for a ZIP catalog's base URL. Direct ZIP dependency\norigins use `origin.type = \"zip-url\"` and `origin.url` instead. These are different\nconfiguration objects."},"3235":{"id":"/registry/sources-16","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#configure-a-catalog","content":"Omit `auth` for public catalogs. Never put a token in a committed manifest:\n`auth` names where the token comes from, not the token itself. Repository auth does\nnot replace system Git authentication."},"3236":{"id":"/registry/sources-17","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`auth.type`"},"3237":{"id":"/registry/sources-18","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Token source"},"3238":{"id":"/registry/sources-19","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Header sent"},"3239":{"id":"/registry/sources-20","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Where it may be configured"},"3240":{"id":"/registry/sources-21","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`pat`"},"3241":{"id":"/registry/sources-22","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`env_var`"},"3242":{"id":"/registry/sources-23","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`Authorization: token …`"},"3243":{"id":"/registry/sources-24","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`skill-project.toml` or user file"},"3244":{"id":"/registry/sources-25","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`bearer`"},"3245":{"id":"/registry/sources-26","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`env_var`"},"3246":{"id":"/registry/sources-27","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`Authorization: Bearer …`"},"3247":{"id":"/registry/sources-28","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`skill-project.toml` or user file"},"3248":{"id":"/registry/sources-29","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`command`"},"3249":{"id":"/registry/sources-30","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"first line printed by `command`"},"3250":{"id":"/registry/sources-31","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`Authorization: Bearer …`"},"3251":{"id":"/registry/sources-32","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"user file only"},"3252":{"id":"/registry/sources-33","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"`bearer` and `command` apply to `http-registry` repositories. With either one, a\nmissing variable or a failing command is an error; FastSkill never retries the\nrequest without credentials. `pat` keeps its existing behaviour and sends no header\nwhen its variable is unset."},"3253":{"id":"/registry/sources-34","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"For a registry that requires a bearer token, name the variable in the manifest:"},"3254":{"id":"/registry/sources-35","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"When the token is short-lived, let a program print it, such as an identity provider\nCLI or a CI job's token exchange. A credential command can only be configured in your\nuser repositories file, `repositories.toml` in FastSkill's configuration directory\n(`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fastskill/` when set, otherwise the platform config directory). A\n`skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused, so cloning a project can never\nmake FastSkill run a program."},"3255":{"id":"/registry/sources-36","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"A user entry replaces a project entry with the same name, for listing, resolution\nand install alike. How the command runs:"},"3256":{"id":"/registry/sources-37","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"It runs directly, without a shell, from FastSkill's configuration directory, and is\nstopped after 30 seconds."},"3257":{"id":"/registry/sources-38","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"The token is the first line of standard output with the trailing line ending\nremoved. Output over 16 KiB, an empty token, or a non-zero exit is an error. Errors\nname the program and its exit status, never the token."},"3258":{"id":"/registry/sources-39","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Standard error reaches your terminal only when there is one, so the command can\nprompt you to sign in. When standard input or standard error is not a terminal,\nFastSkill sets `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0`: the command must then print a token\nwithout prompting, or exit non-zero."},"3259":{"id":"/registry/sources-40","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"It runs at most once per FastSkill process for each repository. The token stays in\nmemory; FastSkill never writes it to disk or prints it."},"3260":{"id":"/registry/sources-41","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"The token is sent only to the origin (scheme, host and port) of `index_url`. A\ndownload on another origin gets no token and must carry its own authorization, such\nas a pre-signed URL. A redirect to another origin is followed without the token, and\na redirect from `https` to `http` is refused."},"3261":{"id":"/registry/sources-42","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"You can also manage sources through the CLI:"},"3262":{"id":"/registry/sources-43","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#registry-authentication","content":"Search results identify the repository, canonical skill ID, version, and install\ncommand. Remote search can fail partially; inspect the exit status and diagnostics\ninstead of treating partial results as a complete catalog response."},"3263":{"id":"/registry/sources-44","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#publish-a-catalog","content":"Git marketplaces and ZIP catalogs describe skills using\nmarketplace.json. HTTP registries expose an\nindex. FastSkill does not provide a CLI publish service;\nhost catalog files and artifacts using your distribution infrastructure."},"3264":{"id":"/registry/sources-45","page_id":"/registry/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/sources#publish-a-catalog","content":"For sharing an already installed set without access to its original sources, use\nbundles. For all repository actions and flags, see\nrepository reference."},"3265":{"id":"/registry/web-ui","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","type":"page","content":"Local browser console","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams","Sources and catalogs"],"tags":[],"url":"/registry/web-ui"},"3266":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-0","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui","content":"Inspect installed skills and manage a project through the optional HTTP server."},"3267":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-1","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/web-ui#write-operations","content":"Write operations"},"3268":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-2","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3269":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-3","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui","content":"Complete the quickstart or open an existing configured project, then run:"},"3270":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-4","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui","content":"Open `http://localhost:8080/`. The console loads project information and the installed\nskills table. Type in the search field to filter the loaded rows; select a skill\nfor its details. Catalog discovery is available through repository commands\nand the registry HTTP endpoints."},"3271":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-5","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#write-operations","content":"The console reads server capabilities before exposing write controls. Start with\nwrite access only when you intend to change installed skills:"},"3272":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-6","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#write-operations","content":"With writes enabled, the console provides an install form, eligible skill updates,\nremoval controls, and an update-all action. Reindexing additionally requires an\nembedding provider. A successful operation refreshes the displayed state; inspect\nerrors when a source cannot resolve or ownership prevents removal."},"3273":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-7","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#write-operations","content":"The server has no built-in authentication. Use it locally, or put authentication\nand network restrictions in front of it when exposing it to other users. Read-only\naccess still reveals skill content. See the security model."},"3274":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-8","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"If the table does not load, check that the server is running in the correct project\nand inspect `fastskill cli doctor` output."},"3275":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-9","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"If write controls are absent, verify that you started with `--enable-write`."},"3276":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-10","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"If reindexing is unavailable, configure the optional embedding provider."},"3277":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-11","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"If a skill cannot be removed, inspect its owners and reconciliation state."},"3278":{"id":"/registry/web-ui-12","page_id":"/registry/web-ui","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/registry/web-ui#troubleshooting","content":"For the HTTP contract, health checks, and server flags, see\nserver reference."},"3279":{"id":"/security/best-practices","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"page","content":"Security Best Practices","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Security"],"tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices"},"3280":{"id":"/security/best-practices-0","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices","content":"Operational guidance for running FastSkill safely: read-only serve, auth proxies, PAT env-var indirection, and locked CI installs."},"3281":{"id":"/security/best-practices-1","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices#overview","content":"Overview"},"3282":{"id":"/security/best-practices-2","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices#running-fastskill-server-serve","content":"Running `fastskill server serve`"},"3283":{"id":"/security/best-practices-3","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"Repository credentials"},"3284":{"id":"/security/best-practices-4","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices#reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"Reproducible installs in CI"},"3285":{"id":"/security/best-practices-5","page_id":"/security/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/best-practices#verify-configuration","content":"Verify configuration"},"3286":{"id":"/security/best-practices-6","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#overview","content":"These are the concrete, source-backed practices for operating FastSkill safely. They follow directly\nfrom the security model: FastSkill is a package manager with no in-app auth, so\nprotection comes from *how you run and expose it*."},"3287":{"id":"/security/best-practices-7","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#running-fastskill-server-serve","content":"**Expose read-only.** For a browsable UI or REST view over your skills, run `fastskill server serve`\n**without** `--enable-write`. Every mutation endpoint returns HTTP 403, so an exposed instance\ncannot install, update, delete, reindex, or refresh anything."},"3288":{"id":"/security/best-practices-8","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#running-fastskill-server-serve","content":"**Only pass `--enable-write` when you mean it.** Enable writes for local skill management from the\nbrowser/API — ideally on `localhost` only. Do not combine `--enable-write` with an open,\nunfronted port."},"3289":{"id":"/security/best-practices-9","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#running-fastskill-server-serve","content":"**Front an exposed port with an authenticating proxy.** `server serve` enforces no authentication of its\nown and is *not* a security boundary. If the port is reachable off your machine, put a reverse\nproxy or sidecar in front that owns authentication, and make sure the app port is not directly\nreachable. Binding a non-loopback address is fine and expected behind such a proxy."},"3290":{"id":"/security/best-practices-10","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#running-fastskill-server-serve","content":"**Use the health probes for orchestration**, not for security: `GET /healthz` (liveness) and\n`GET /readyz` (readiness)."},"3291":{"id":"/security/best-practices-11","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"**Use PAT env-var indirection.** Reference tokens by environment variable in\n`skill-project.toml`, never inline:"},"3292":{"id":"/security/best-practices-12","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"**Never commit plaintext tokens.** Keep them in your shell profile, CI secret store, or a secrets\nmanager. Commit `skill-project.toml`; keep the token value out of the repo."},"3293":{"id":"/security/best-practices-13","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"**Registry credentials stay on the registry origin.** FastSkill sends the configured PAT or\nbearer token to index and artifact URLs only when they have the same scheme, host, and port as\n`index_url`. Use a pre-signed URL or separately authenticated delivery layer when artifacts are\nhosted on another origin."},"3294":{"id":"/security/best-practices-14","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"**Prefer short-lived tokens from a credential command.** Configure it with\n`fastskill repo add --user --auth-type command --credential-command <program>`; it is saved to\nyour user `repositories.toml`, never to the project. In CI and hooks the command sees\n`FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0`, so it must print a token without prompting or exit non-zero."},"3295":{"id":"/security/best-practices-15","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#repository-credentials","content":"**Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` via secrets** where semantic search / reindex is used. If it is unset,\nembedding-based features silently skip rather than failing — but do not paste the key into config\nor version control."},"3296":{"id":"/security/best-practices-16","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"**Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`.**"},"3297":{"id":"/security/best-practices-17","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"**Use `fastskill project install --lock` in CI** so builds install the exact locked versions rather than\nre-resolving. This makes installs reproducible and verifiable across environments. See the\ncheatsheet for the full manifest workflow."},"3298":{"id":"/security/best-practices-18","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#verify-configuration","content":"Run `fastskill cli doctor` (add `--json` for machine output) to confirm the skills directory,\n`skill-project.toml`, embedding configuration, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, and auth token are set up as\nexpected before deploying. See Debugging."},"3299":{"id":"/security/best-practices-19","page_id":"/security/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/best-practices#verify-configuration","content":"FastSkill deliberately has **no audit-logging feature** and **no in-app auth** — do not rely on it\nfor either. Request logging, authentication, and network policy belong to the proxy and platform\nthat front an exposed instance."},"3300":{"id":"/security/model","page_id":"/security/model","type":"page","content":"Security Model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Security"],"tags":[],"url":"/security/model"},"3301":{"id":"/security/model-0","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model","content":"How FastSkill treats trust boundaries: read-only-by-default serve, no in-app auth, env-var token indirection, and reproducible locked installs."},"3302":{"id":"/security/model-1","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#overview","content":"Overview"},"3303":{"id":"/security/model-2","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#fastskill-server-serve-is-read-only-by-default","content":"`fastskill server serve` is read-only by default"},"3304":{"id":"/security/model-3","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"`server serve` is not a security boundary"},"3305":{"id":"/security/model-4","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"Repository credentials: env-var indirection"},"3306":{"id":"/security/model-5","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#reproducible-verifiable-installs","content":"Reproducible, verifiable installs"},"3307":{"id":"/security/model-6","page_id":"/security/model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"What FastSkill does not provide"},"3308":{"id":"/security/model-7","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#overview","content":"FastSkill is a skill **package manager**, not a runtime. It installs, indexes, and serves skill\ndirectories; it does **not** execute skills, so there is no sandbox, no resource governor, and no\nper-request audit log to speak of. Its security model is about two things: what the `fastskill server serve`\nHTTP surface lets a caller do, and how repository credentials are handled."},"3309":{"id":"/security/model-8","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#fastskill-server-serve-is-read-only-by-default","content":"Per ADR-0003, `fastskill server serve` mounts **only read endpoints** unless you start it with\n`--enable-write`. Reads (list/get skills, `POST /api/v1/search`, `POST /api/v1/resolve`,\n`GET /api/v1/status`, registry browse, manifest reads, the dashboard) are always available."},"3310":{"id":"/security/model-9","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#fastskill-server-serve-is-read-only-by-default","content":"Every state-changing endpoint — install, update, delete, reindex, registry refresh, manifest\nwrites — returns **HTTP 403** when writes are disabled:"},"3311":{"id":"/security/model-10","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#fastskill-server-serve-is-read-only-by-default","content":"\"Anything that is not a pure read is gated\" — reindex and registry refresh are included because they\nare side-effecting (disk, network, embedding-API cost), not just because they are destructive. This\nis one switch: `--enable-write` enables all mutations at once. See the\n`server serve` reference."},"3312":{"id":"/security/model-11","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"FastSkill enforces **no authentication of its own**. There is no token endpoint, and API routes\nrequire no `Authorization` or `x-api-key` header. It handles no identity and no per-user\nauthorization by design."},"3313":{"id":"/security/model-12","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"**Run it local-first.** The default bind is `localhost` — a single operator viewing their own\nskills on their own machine."},"3314":{"id":"/security/model-13","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"**Front it with an authenticating proxy if you expose it.** If the port is reachable on a shared\nor untrusted network, put a reverse proxy or sidecar in front that owns request authentication,\nand ensure the app port is not directly reachable. FastSkill will not police the bind address for\nyou, and binding a non-loopback address is the normal, expected configuration behind such a proxy."},"3315":{"id":"/security/model-14","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"Combined with the read-only default, an exposed instance started **without** `--enable-write` cannot\nbe used to mutate state even before the proxy is considered. Reaching a destructive endpoint\nunauthenticated requires the operator to have *both* enabled writes *and* exposed the port with no\nfronting proxy — a deliberate double opt-out."},"3316":{"id":"/security/model-15","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#server-serve-is-not-a-security-boundary","content":"A read-only exposed instance still **discloses skill data** to anyone who reaches it. That is the\noperator's call when they open the port; it is a disclosure consideration, not a mutation risk."},"3317":{"id":"/security/model-16","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"HTTP registries can authenticate with a **PAT or bearer token referenced by environment variable**.\nGit sources use system Git credentials. Tokens are not written into the manifest:"},"3318":{"id":"/security/model-17","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"FastSkill reads the token from `TEAM_REGISTRY_TOKEN` at runtime. Commit `skill-project.toml`; keep\nthe token in your shell profile, CI secrets, or a secrets manager. Never commit a plaintext token."},"3319":{"id":"/security/model-18","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"A registry that requires an OAuth bearer token uses `auth = { type = \"bearer\", env_var = \"…\" }`\ninstead, and FastSkill sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. When the token is short-lived, a\n**credential command** can print it (`auth = { type = \"command\", command = [...] }`):"},"3320":{"id":"/security/model-19","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"**Only user configuration may name a command.** It lives in `repositories.toml` in FastSkill's\nconfiguration directory. A `skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused, so a cloned\nrepository can never make FastSkill run a program."},"3321":{"id":"/security/model-20","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"**It runs without a shell**, from FastSkill's configuration directory, with a 30-second timeout,\nat most once per process for each repository. The token stays in memory; it is never written to\ndisk, logs or error messages."},"3322":{"id":"/security/model-21","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"**Non-interactive runs are flagged.** When standard input or standard error is not a terminal,\nthe command sees `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0` and must not prompt."},"3323":{"id":"/security/model-22","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"**The token stays on the registry origin.** It is sent only to the scheme, host and port of\n`index_url`. A redirect to another origin drops it, and a redirect from `https` to `http` is\nrefused."},"3324":{"id":"/security/model-23","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#repository-credentials-env-var-indirection","content":"**Missing credentials fail closed.** An unset `bearer` variable or a failing command is an error,\nnever an unauthenticated retry. `pat` keeps its existing behaviour."},"3325":{"id":"/security/model-24","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#reproducible-verifiable-installs","content":"`fastskill project install` resolves the manifest and writes a lockfile (`skills.lock`, or\n`global-skills.lock` with `--global`). `fastskill project install --lock` installs the **exact** versions\nrecorded in the lock, giving reproducible and verifiable installs for CI and locked environments.\nCommit both `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`."},"3326":{"id":"/security/model-25","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"To set expectations honestly, FastSkill has **no**:"},"3327":{"id":"/security/model-26","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"sandboxed execution environment (it does not run skills),"},"3328":{"id":"/security/model-27","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"resource limits or execution monitoring,"},"3329":{"id":"/security/model-28","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"built-in request audit log,"},"3330":{"id":"/security/model-29","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"in-app authentication, identity, or per-user authorization."},"3331":{"id":"/security/model-30","page_id":"/security/model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/model#what-fastskill-does-not-provide","content":"For deployed exposure, those responsibilities live in the surrounding infrastructure (proxy,\nnetwork policy, secrets management)."},"3332":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"page","content":"Manifests, locks, and scope","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Manage skills","Skills and projects"],"tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system"},"3333":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-0","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system","content":"Declare sources and understand what FastSkill restores for a project or user."},"3334":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-1","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-configuration","content":"Project configuration"},"3335":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-2","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"Manifest composition"},"3336":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-3","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#dependency-origins","content":"Dependency origins"},"3337":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-4","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#groups","content":"Groups"},"3338":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-5","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#locked-restoration-and-updates","content":"Locked restoration and updates"},"3339":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-6","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-and-global-scope","content":"Project and global scope"},"3340":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-7","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#author-configuration","content":"Author configuration"},"3341":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-8","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-configuration","content":"A project's `skill-project.toml` defines the installation directory and desired\nskills. FastSkill finds it by walking up from your working directory. Paths in the\nmanifest are relative to the manifest directory, not the calling shell's directory."},"3342":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-9","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-configuration","content":"Use the quickstart to create this local source. `skill add` writes a\ndependency and installs it. Editing the manifest manually requires a subsequent\n`project install` to apply it."},"3343":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-10","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-configuration","content":"FastSkill refuses a manifest with a key it does not recognise under\n`[tool.fastskill]`, so a misspelt setting fails loudly instead of being ignored.\nOther tables, such as `[tool.<other-tool>]`, are left alone and kept on save."},"3344":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-11","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"Reference a reusable team Manifest without copying its dependencies:"},"3345":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-12","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"A reference may name the file or its containing directory. References are recursive and their\npaths are relative to the Manifest containing the declaration. Dependencies inside each referenced\nManifest keep their own path base, so a shared Manifest may combine Git, repository, ZIP URL, and\nshared-filesystem origins normally."},"3346":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-13","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"`project install` resolves all composed roots into the consuming project's `skills.lock`. Repeated\nidentical declarations are deduplicated. Missing files, cycles, or different origins/groups for the\nsame skill ID are errors and stop installation before managed state changes."},"3347":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-14","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"A composed Manifest's `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` join the consuming project's for\nresolution, so a shared `repository` origin finds the catalog its own Manifest names. A local\nrepository `path` is relative to the Manifest that declares it. When two Manifests define the same\nrepository name differently, installation stops and asks you to rename one; identical definitions\nare merged. `fastskill repo` commands list and edit only the project's own repositories."},"3348":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-15","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"Only dependencies and repositories are taken from a composed Manifest. Its `skills_directory`,\n`[tool.fastskill.eval]` and `[tool.fastskill.server]` are ignored on purpose: those settings belong\nto the consuming project."},"3349":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-16","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#manifest-composition","content":"Manifest composition is supported in author-controlled project manifests. Installed or fetched\nskill packages must declare dependencies directly; their manifest references are rejected before\nany referenced file is read. This prevents packages from importing host project files."},"3350":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-17","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#dependency-origins","content":"These are examples of source declarations, not publicly available packages:"},"3351":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-18","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#dependency-origins","content":"A repository origin refers to a configured catalog. See source configuration.\nUse `skill add` to produce declarations from actual sources rather than guessing IDs.\nEditable local dependencies link to their source and are intentionally mutable;\nother local dependencies are copied and checked against locked integrity evidence."},"3352":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-19","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#groups","content":"Groups select optional roots. Required transitive dependencies remain part of the\nselected roots' installation closure."},"3353":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-20","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#groups","content":"Use one group selection mode per invocation. A group-limited lock may not cover\nroots excluded from that resolution; `--lock` cannot resolve missing coverage."},"3354":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-21","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#locked-restoration-and-updates","content":"`skills.lock` records the resolved result of local and composed Manifest roots: origins, versions, Git commits, content digests,\ndependency edges, groups, covered roots, bundle ownership, and overrides. It is\ngenerated by FastSkill; do not hand-write a partial lockfile."},"3355":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-22","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#locked-restoration-and-updates","content":"A content digest names the exact files of a skill directory and is written as\n`sha256-tree-v2:<hex>`. A lockfile from an earlier release may hold 64-character digests\nwithout that prefix; they are still verified, with a warning, and are replaced when fastskill\nnext rewrites that entry. fastskill releases before this format report a checksum mismatch on\nthe new form, so upgrade every machine and CI job that shares the lockfile."},"3356":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-23","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#locked-restoration-and-updates","content":"Ordinary installation reuses compatible locked selections and resolves roots that\nlack coverage. `--lock` verifies and restores the recorded selection without\nchanging lock bytes. Updates deliberately resolve changes within the declared\nconstraints; exact pins stay pinned unless explicitly changed."},"3357":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-24","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#locked-restoration-and-updates","content":"Commit the manifest and lock together. Local sources and cached bundle artifacts\nmust also be available to recipients. `--offline` prevents network access; it\nrequires all necessary verified inputs locally and does not make remote dependencies\nportable by itself. See bundle distribution."},"3358":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-25","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-and-global-scope","content":"Project operations use the manifest's installation directory. `--skills-dir`\noverrides that destination when supported. Global operations use the user-level\nskill set and `global-skills.lock`; the default directory is\n`~/.config/fastskill/skills` on Unix."},"3359":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-26","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#project-and-global-scope","content":"A global FastSkill directory is not automatically an agent's discovery directory.\nConfirm the location your agent reads or access global skills through MCP.\nGlobal lock restoration does not require a project manifest."},"3360":{"id":"/skill-management/manifest-system-27","page_id":"/skill-management/manifest-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/manifest-system#author-configuration","content":"Within a skill directory, `skill-project.toml` can also carry author metadata and\nskill dependencies. A standalone skill can begin with only `SKILL.md`; separate\nproject configuration controls where consumers install it. See\nskill validation and project init."},"3361":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"page","content":"Reconcile project skill state","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Manage skills","Skills and projects"],"tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation"},"3362":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-0","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation","content":"Compare declared, locked, and installed skill state and enforce it in CI."},"3363":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-1","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"Reconcile project skill state"},"3364":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-2","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#human-readable-checks","content":"Human-readable checks"},"3365":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-3","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Reconciliation values"},"3366":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-4","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#json-schema","content":"JSON schema"},"3367":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-5","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#group-scoped-checks","content":"Group-scoped checks"},"3368":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-6","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#ci-example","content":"CI example"},"3369":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-7","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#repair-workflow","content":"Repair workflow"},"3370":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-8","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#global-state","content":"Global state"},"3371":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-9","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"fastskill compares three sources of truth:"},"3372":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-10","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"`skill-project.toml` records direct intent, groups, and source constraints."},"3373":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-11","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"`skills.lock` records the resolved closure, versions, origins, ownership, and integrity data."},"3374":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-12","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"The skills directory contains the installed files an agent reads."},"3375":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-13","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconcile-project-skill-state","content":"`fastskill skill list` joins those sources into one row per skill. `fastskill skill list --check`\nuses the same rows and returns nonzero when selected managed state needs reconciliation."},"3376":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-14","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#human-readable-checks","content":"The detailed source path is the recorded origin path or URL, not the installed destination.\nEditable installs use the human-readable `editable` flag."},"3377":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-15","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"The `reconciliation` field is the canonical machine-readable status. Values can include:"},"3378":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-16","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Value"},"3379":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-17","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Meaning"},"3380":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-18","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`managed-blocked`"},"3381":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-19","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"The managed state blocks the installed content's digest."},"3382":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-20","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`managed-not-allowed`"},"3383":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-21","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"The managed state allows only listed content, and the installed content isn't listed."},"3384":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-22","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`ok`"},"3385":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-23","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Selected state agrees and managed content passes integrity checks."},"3386":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-24","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`excluded`"},"3387":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-25","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"A group filter excluded the owning root."},"3388":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-26","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`missing-lock`"},"3389":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-27","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Declared intent has no resolved lock entry."},"3390":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-28","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`missing-content`"},"3391":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-29","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Managed content is absent from the skills directory."},"3392":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-30","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`intent-mismatch`"},"3393":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-31","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Manifest intent and locked origin differ."},"3394":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-32","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`revision-mismatch`"},"3395":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-33","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed and locked versions differ."},"3396":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-34","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`content-mismatch`"},"3397":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-35","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed managed content differs from its digest."},"3398":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-36","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`integrity-error`"},"3399":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-37","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"Installed content could not be verified."},"3400":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-38","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"`insufficient-integrity`"},"3401":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-39","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#reconciliation-values","content":"The lock lacks evidence required for a reliable check."},"3402":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-40","