content":"Overview"},"3458":{"id":"/testing/framework-2","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"Configure evals"},"3459":{"id":"/testing/framework-3","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"The eval subcommands"},"3460":{"id":"/testing/framework-4","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"See also"},"3461":{"id":"/testing/framework-5","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#overview","content":"The way you test a skill in FastSkill is `fastskill eval`. You define eval cases in your project\nmanifest, run them against an agent, and score the results. There is no separate unit/mock harness —\neval is the testing framework."},"3462":{"id":"/testing/framework-6","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"Evals are declared under `[tool.fastskill.eval]` in `skill-project.toml`:"},"3463":{"id":"/testing/framework-7","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`prompts` — path to a CSV of prompt cases to run."},"3464":{"id":"/testing/framework-8","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`checks` — path to a TOML file of checks applied to each result."},"3465":{"id":"/testing/framework-9","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`timeout_seconds` — per-case timeout."},"3466":{"id":"/testing/framework-10","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`fail_on_missing_agent` — when `true`, eval fails instead of skipping if the agent isn't found."},"3467":{"id":"/testing/framework-11","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Command"},"3468":{"id":"/testing/framework-12","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"What it does"},"3469":{"id":"/testing/framework-13","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval validate`"},"3470":{"id":"/testing/framework-14","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Validates the eval configuration and referenced files before running"},"3471":{"id":"/testing/framework-15","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval run`"},"3472":{"id":"/testing/framework-16","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Runs the eval cases against an agent"},"3473":{"id":"/testing/framework-17","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval report`"},"3474":{"id":"/testing/framework-18","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Shows a report for a completed eval run"},"3475":{"id":"/testing/framework-19","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval score`"},"3476":{"id":"/testing/framework-20","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Scores results"},"3477":{"id":"/testing/framework-21","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Eval output supports `--format table|json` (no grid/xml for eval)."},"3478":{"id":"/testing/framework-22","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Start by pinning down what \"good\" looks like in your `checks.toml`, then iterate: `eval run` →\n`eval report` → adjust the skill → repeat."},"3479":{"id":"/testing/framework-23","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"Evals & quality overview — the quality workflow and concepts."},"3480":{"id":"/testing/framework-24","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"eval command reference — full flags and output details."},"3481":{"id":"/tool-calling/development","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"page","content":"MCP Tool Calling","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","MCP tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development"},"3482":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-0","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development","content":"Expose FastSkill to agents as MCP tools with `fastskill mcp serve` (read-only by default, `--enable-write` to allow mutation), and wire them into Claude Code, Cursor, and other agents with `fastskill mcp install`."},"3483":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-1","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#overview","content":"Overview"},"3484":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-2","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#serve-fastskill-as-an-mcp-server","content":"Serve FastSkill as an MCP server"},"3485":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-3","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#write-access","content":"Write access"},"3486":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-4","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#transports","content":"Transports"