"3576":2138},"orderedDocs":[[1365,"-"],[1370,"-"],[1375,"-"],[1380,"-"],[1385,"-"],[1390,"-"],[1395,"-"],[1400,"-"],[1405,"-"],[1446,"-"],[1451,"-"],[1564,"—"],[1947,"—"],[1956,"—"],[2200,"—"],[2291,"—"],[2308,"—"],[2321,"—"],[2334,"—"],[2581,"—"],[2295,"— (`true` = pattern must appear, `false` = must NOT appear)"],[2269,"— (omit to match *any* skill invocation)"],[3311,"\"Anything that is not a pure read is gated\" — reindex and registry refresh are included because they\nare side-effecting (disk, network, embedding-API cost), not just because they are destructive. This\nis one switch: `--enable-write` enables all mutations at once. See the\n`server serve` reference."],[1165,"\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set\""],[1166,"\"Permission denied\" on database"],[2000,"\"Project-level init requires --skills-dir\""],[1999,"\"skill-project.toml already exists. Use --force to overwrite.\""],[2235,"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"],[1204,"**`--progress` / `--no-progress`**: Force the progress bar on, or suppress it and show only the final summary"],[3451,"**`auth_token` failing** — set `FASTSKILL_AUTH_TOKEN` (or `FASTSKILL_TOKEN`) if you use a private\nregistry."],[1240,"**`build-cache.json`** — the change-detection cache:"],[465,"**`cache clean`**: To reclaim disk space after finishing with skills from a source no longer\nin use, or as routine cleanup on a machine used for many short-lived projects."],[464,"**`cache info`**: Before a `clean`, to see what is actually taking up space, or when disk\nusage seems higher than expected."],[3450,"**`embedding_config` / `api_key` failing** — add `[tool.fastskill.embedding]` and set\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`; without them semantic search and reindex are disabled (they skip silently, they\ndon't error)."],[1236,"**`index.db`** — the vector index:"],[3449,"**`project_toml` failing** — run `fastskill project init` to create `skill-project.toml`."],[2257,"**`should_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."],[2230,"**`true`**"],[1249,"**100 skills**: \\~$0.001 (less than 1 cent)"],[2737,"**A new version is written only when a step is accepted**, so version numbers count\n*accepted steps*, not steps. Once any step has been rejected they no longer line up with\nstep indices: if step 0 is rejected and step 1 accepted, step 1's diff is\n`skill_v0000.md → skill_v0001.md`, not `v0001 → v0002`."],[3026,"**Access Control**: Registry access is controlled by authentication"],[2067,"**Add skills**: `fastskill skill add <skill-id>` (registry, Git, or local path)."],[654,"**Advisory judge rows.** A `judge:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."],[1231,"**API Key Issues**: Check `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable"],[3027,"**Audit Trail**: Publishing history is maintained automatically"],[228,"**Authors**: init, validate, eval, and ship skills via the platform."],[2936,"**Automatic rebuilding keeps the index fresh.** After `skill add`, `project install`,\n`skill update`, or `skill remove`, FastSkill\nreindexes automatically (unless `auto_reindex = false` or `--no-reindex`, and only when an\nembedding provider is available), so `resolve` reflects the current skill set."],[231,"**Automation**: `project install --lock` and reproducible installs in CI."],[1248,"**Average skill**: \\~500 tokens"],[1431,"**Behavior**:"],[626,"**Benchmark**"],[3024,"**Blob Storage**: Artifacts are stored securely with checksum verification"],[2107,"**Case-based evals** with `fastskill eval` to test expected behavior against prompts and rubrics"],[2064,"**Cause**: `--yes` was used at a project root without a skills directory.\n**Solution**: add `--skills-dir <path>`, or drop `--yes` to be prompted."],[2063,"**Cause**: a `skill-project.toml` is already present.\n**Solution**: pass `--force` to overwrite it, or remove the file first."],[337,"**Cause**: Another `fastskill` command is currently running and has acquired an exclusive lock on the lock file."],[2066,"**Cause**: the current directory is not writable.\n**Solution**: fix permissions or run in a directory where you have write access."],[349,"**Cause**: The lock file was manually edited incorrectly, interrupted during write, or corrupted by a bug."],[362,"**Cause**: The system cannot determine the standard config directory for your platform."],[2065,"**Cause**: the version (from `--set-version` or `SKILL.md`) is not valid semver.\n**Solution**: use a semver string such as `1.0.0`."],[2061,"**Changing the embedding model invalidates your index.** Vectors from different\nmodels are not comparable — and often not even the same length. After switching\nmodels, run `fastskill index rebuild` before searching, or results will be meaningless."],[2466,"**Check environment readiness**"],[1538,"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."],[370,"**Check permissions**:"],[2010,"**Checks for an existing file**: refuses to overwrite `skill-project.toml` unless `--force` is given."],[2260,"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."],[2836,"**Checks TOML*&#x2A; — the grading rules that score each response. &#x2A;(Optional, but without it there is no real grading signal — see below.)*"],[2677,"**Checks**"],[3025,"**Checksum Verification**: All downloads include SHA256 checksums"],[3000,"**cksum**: SHA256 checksum of the ZIP artifact"],[2433,"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."],[226,"**CLI**: single entry point for installs, checks, search, and evals."],[3296,"**Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`.**"],[373,"**Commit project lock to git**:"],[1239,"**Content**: Metadata and embeddings used by semantic search"],[1242,"**Content**: Per-skill file hashes used to decide which skills changed since the last run"],[2007,"**Context detection**: `project init` detects whether you're in a skill directory or a project root:"],[3132,"**Converts to internal format** for processing by:"],[369,"**Create the directory manually**:"],[726,"**Creates File**: Writes `skill-project.toml` with basic structure and commented examples"],[2464,"**Cursor doesn't see a skill**"],[2044,"**Custom**: any path you pass via `--skills-dir` or the prompt"],[2043,"**Default**: `.claude/skills`"],[1202,"**Default**: Shows a live progress bar with completion percentage (when stdout is a TTY)"],[2232,"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."],[2999,"**deps**: Dependencies (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[717,"**Detects Context**: Determines if you're in a skill directory (with SKILL.md) or a project directory"],[229,"**Developers**: install, list, read, search for what agents load."],[874,"**Development Mode** (with `skill-project.toml`):"],[363,"**Diagnosis**:"],[2468,"**Direct skill discovery** — Cursor reads installed skills from the skills directory, no sync step"],[374,"**Don't commit global lock**:"],[376,"**Don't manually edit lock files** unless you understand the TOML schema"],[3004,"**download\\_url**: URL to download the ZIP artifact"],[2931,"**Embeddings power ranking when available.** With `OPENAI_API_KEY` set (and\n`[tool.fastskill.embedding]` configured), FastSkill ranks skills semantically using the embedding\nindex."],[2681,"**Epoch**"],[361,"**Error**: `Global config directory unavailable: ...`"],[336,"**Error**: `Lock file is held by another process: /path/to/skills.lock`"],[650,"**Errored trials.** A trial with outcome `error` still carries check results, because the checks ran, over an empty trace. Every negative expectation and every tool-call ceiling passed there vacuously, so folding them would report an outage as perfect restraint. They are dropped from every rate and counted separately."],[652,"**Estimated cost.** Only the vendor-reported figure is summed. When no trial reported one, the line reads \"not reported\" rather than `$0.00`."],[2898,"**Example `checks.toml`:**"],[2870,"**Example `suite.csv`** (has both `train` and `selection` rows, plus a held-out `test` row):"],[1918,"**Example output:**"],[454,"**Example output**:"],[1356,"**Example Output**:"],[1436,"**Example Output**:"],[1504,"**Example Output**:"],[1515,"**Example Output**:"],[3008,"**Example:**"],[1533,"**Example**:"],[3169,"**Example**: If skill-project.toml has `version = \"2.0.0\"` but SKILL.md has `version: \"1.0.0\"`, the marketplace.json will use `\"2.0.0\"`. Similarly, if skill-project.toml has `author = \"New Author\"`, it will override the author from SKILL.md. The `name` field always comes from SKILL.md frontmatter for display purposes, as it is not present in skill-project.toml."],[1461,"**Exit codes**:"],[3287,"**Expose read-only.** For a browsable UI or REST view over your skills, run `fastskill server serve`\n**without** `--enable-write`. Every mutation endpoint returns HTTP 403, so an exposed instance\ncannot install, update, delete, reindex, or refresh anything."],[718,"**Extracts Metadata**: If SKILL.md exists, extracts version, description, and author from YAML frontmatter"],[3001,"**features**: Feature flags (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[1113,"**File permissions**: Ensure you have read/write permissions for skill directories."],[1241,"**Format**: JSON"],[1237,"**Format**: SQLite database"],[3289,"**Front an exposed port with an authenticating proxy.** `server serve` enforces no authentication of its\nown and is *not* a security boundary. If the port is reachable off your machine, put a reverse\nproxy or sidecar in front that owns authentication, and make sure the app port is not directly\nreachable. Binding a non-loopback address is fine and expected behind such a proxy."],[3314,"**Front it with an authenticating proxy if you expose it.** If the port is reachable on a shared\nor untrusted network, put a reverse proxy or sidecar in front that owns request authentication,\nand ensure the app port is not directly reachable. FastSkill will not police the bind address for\nyou, and binding a non-loopback address is the normal, expected configuration behind such a proxy."],[2605,"**Gate metric options** (per case, then averaged across the split — see\nSetup):"],[2679,"**Gate metric**"],[724,"**Generates Skill ID**: Uses the current directory name as the skill ID"],[3191,"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."],[3052,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[3056,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[1411,"**git-marketplace**: Git repository with `marketplace.json` for skill discovery"],[335,"**Global lock**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\fastskill\\global-skills.lock` (Windows)"],[1490,"**Grid**: Human-readable columnar layout with the same fields as table"],[3192,"**HTTP registry**: an HTTP index and downloadable skill artifacts."],[1416,"**http-registry**: HTTP-based registry with flat skill index"],[2983,"**ID** → Second directory level (the package name, must not contain slashes, e.g., \"web-scraper\")"],[2905,"**If you omit `checks` from `optimize.toml` entirely, there is no grading signal at all**: with zero checks configured, every case's result list is empty, and an empty list scores `1.0` under every `gate_metric` (vacuously — \"zero required checks passed\" is trivially true). In that configuration every candidate patch looks perfect, so the gate has nothing meaningful to accept or reject on. Always configure `checks` for a real run."],[3180,"**Include all metadata**: Provide tags, capabilities, and author information"],[2935,"**Incremental index rebuilding.** A change-detection cache (`.fastskill/build-cache.json`) lets\nFastSkill\nre-embed only what actually changed, so keeping the index current is cheap."],[2069,"**Index for search**: `fastskill index rebuild` (requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`)."],[2068,"**Install from the manifest**: `fastskill project install`."],[868,"**Installs Skills**: Stages and commits each overlapping dependency closure as one recovery unit"],[758,"**Invalid IDs:**"],[744,"**Invalid versions:**"],[3321,"**It runs without a shell**, from FastSkill's configuration directory, with a 30-second timeout,\nat most once per process for each repository. The token stays in memory; it is never written to\ndisk, logs or error messages."],[1491,"**JSON**: Machine-readable array with fields: id, scope, name, description, latest\\_version, published\\_at, and optionally versions array"],[653,"**Judge errors and excluded trials.** A trial whose judgment errored contributes nothing to a `judge_score` — not a zero — and is counted in `totals.judge_errors`. A trial a gated judge could not judge is counted in `totals.judge_excluded_trials`."],[628,"**Judges**"],[378,"**Keep FastSkill up to date** to get lock file improvements and bug fixes"],[3178,"**Keep it updated**: Regenerate `marketplace.json` when skills change"],[2932,"**Keyword fallback otherwise.** If no embedding provider is configured, semantic ranking silently\nskips and resolution falls back to keyword matching — the endpoint still returns results, it just\nranks them without embeddings."],[342,"**Kill the conflicting process**:"],[1246,"**Large repositories** (1000+ skills): 10-30 minutes"],[3003,"**links**: Reserved for future use"],[365,"**Linux/macOS**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock`"],[862,"**Loads Dependencies**: Reads `[dependencies]` section from `skill-project.toml`"],[2459,"**Loads the full `SKILL.md`** for relevant skills to get instructions and parameters —\nthe same content `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` prints."],[3194,"**Local catalog**: skill content and catalog metadata on disk."],[2934,"**Local vector index.** Skill embeddings are stored in a local SQLite vector index (path set by\n`index_path` under `[tool.fastskill.embedding]`), so resolution queries run against on-disk vectors\nwith no external service call at query time."],[1423,"**local**: Local filesystem path"],[861,"**Locates Project File**: Finds `skill-project.toml` at project root or walks up directory tree"],[2458,"**Matches task requirements** against each skill's `description` frontmatter."],[2469,"**MCP access** — register the FastSkill MCP server for tool-based access inside Cursor"],[1245,"**Medium repositories** (100 skills): 2-5 minutes"],[3324,"**Missing credentials fail closed.** An unset `bearer` variable or a failing command is an error,\nnever an unauthenticated retry. `pat` keeps its existing behaviour."],[2997,"**name**: Skill identifier"],[1233,"**Network Issues**: Check internet connectivity"],[3292,"**Never commit plaintext tokens.** Keep them in your shell profile, CI secret store, or a secrets\nmanager. Commit `skill-project.toml`; keep the token value out of the repo."],[3322,"**Non-interactive runs are flagged.** When standard input or standard error is not a terminal,\nthe command sees `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0` and must not prompt."],[651,"**Not-observable checks.** A check whose evidence the backend cannot produce records `passed: false` for older readers. It is excluded rather than counted as a failure."],[2583,"**Note on `aggregate_group_size` and `gate_trials`:** unlike the other numeric fields, these two\nare not checked by `fastskill`'s own config validation. A `0` value parses fine and passes\n`fastskill optimization run`'s validation step, then fails once the training loop starts, as\n`OPTIMIZE_TRAINING_FAILED: TEXTGRAD_INVALID_CONFIG: gate_trials must be > 0` (or the\nequivalent for `aggregate_group_size`) — confirmed by running the binary with `gate_trials = 0`."],[2745,"**Note:** `best_skill.md` is the highest-scoring skill document seen across all accepted\nsteps — not necessarily the final step. If the last few steps were rejected, it reflects the\nbest earlier checkpoint. A run where nothing was accepted exports the seed document, with\nthe optimizer's protected-region markers added."],[2817,"**Note:** Resume uses the config stored *inside* the run directory, not your original config file. This ensures the run is reproducible regardless of changes you may have made to the config since starting."],[3156,"**Note**: `skill-project.toml` provides metadata support (id, version, description, author, tags, capabilities, download\\_url). The `id` field is required and must not contain slashes. The `name` field is not used in skill-project.toml - skill names for display come from `SKILL.md` frontmatter only. All fields in skill-project.toml take priority over SKILL.md frontmatter."],[3060,"**Note**: FastSkill will automatically try the Claude Code standard location (`.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`) first, then fall back to the root location if not found. Both locations are supported."],[3149,"**Note**: The output file is automatically placed at `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (unless `--output` is specified)."],[3288,"**Only pass `--enable-write` when you mean it.** Enable writes for local skill management from the\nbrowser/API — ideally on `localhost` only. Do not combine `--enable-write` with an open,\nunfronted port."],[3320,"**Only user configuration may name a command.** It lives in `repositories.toml` in FastSkill's\nconfiguration directory. A `skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused, so a cloned\nrepository can never make FastSkill run a program."],[227,"**Optional `server serve`**: HTTP API and UI on your machine for browsing and integrations."],[2471,"**Optional semantic search** — `fastskill index rebuild` + `fastskill skill search --local` when an embedding provider is configured"],[3140,"**Options:**"],[916,"**Options** (every subcommand):"],[455,"**Options**:"],[459,"**Options**:"],[1358,"**Options**:"],[1439,"**Options**:"],[1481,"**Options**:"],[3023,"**Organization Structure**: Skills are organized by publishing organization"],[1353,"**Output Format**:"],[1488,"**Output Format**:"],[1509,"**Output Format**:\nDisplays a table of versions with:"],[1497,"**Output Format**:\nDisplays comprehensive skill information including:"],[215,"**Package manager and operational toolkit for AI agent skills.** fastskill enables discovery, installation, versioning, and deployment of skills at scale. It implements the same `SKILL.md` conventions used by Claude Code–compatible agents, and adds **manifests**, **lockfiles**, **self-contained team bundles**, **validation*&#x2A;, optional &#x2A;*`fastskill eval`** runs, and **search**. Modern agents read installed skills directly from the skills directory — no metadata-file sync step."],[1494,"**Parameters**:"],[1506,"**Parameters**:"],[3131,"**Parses Claude Code format** directly"],[1112,"**Path issue**: Ensure FastSkill is installed and in your PATH."],[1234,"**Permission Issues**: Ensure write access to skills directory"],[1222,"**Piped output**: No progress bar (falls back to simple text)"],[1115,"**Port conflicts**: Check if the default port (8080) is available."],[2108,"**Portfolio analysis** with `fastskill analysis` to inspect coverage, overlap, clusters, and duplicates across installed skills"],[3294,"**Prefer short-lived tokens from a credential command.** Configure it with\n`fastskill repo add --user --auth-type command --credential-command <program>`; it is saved to\nyour user `repositories.toml`, never to the project. In CI and hooks the command sees\n`FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0`, so it must print a token without prompting or exit non-zero."],[344,"**Prevention**: Avoid running multiple `fastskill` commands simultaneously in the same project or with the same global scope."],[719,"**Prioritizes Inputs**: Uses values in this priority order:"],[1426,"**Priority-Based Conflict Resolution**:"],[875,"**Production Mode** (with `skills.lock`):"],[334,"**Project lock**: `skills.lock` in your project root"],[2009,"**Project-level**: run at a project root — writes `[dependencies]` for skill consumers. A skills directory is required (via `--skills-dir`, or the prompt)."],[3005,"**published\\_at**: ISO 8601 timestamp of publication"],[1232,"**Rate Limits**: Wait before retrying (reindex already runs sequentially)"],[2011,"**Reads `SKILL.md`** (if present): pulls `version`, `description`, and `author` from the frontmatter."],[2457,"**Reads available skills** from the skills directory (and the FastSkill MCP server, if\nregistered)."],[1223,"**Redirected output**: No progress bar"],[377,"**Regenerate rather than fix** if the lock becomes corrupted"],[3293,"**Registry credentials stay on the registry origin.** FastSkill sends the configured PAT or\nbearer token to index and artifact URLs only when they have the same scheme,