 other member against its installed directory.\nThe release digest is recomputed from the new member digests."],[2346,"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."],[655,"A case whose every trial errored is named in the output, and a metric that matched nothing **fails the command** even under `--no-fail`: a mistyped case pattern would otherwise make a gate quietly disappear. Check results that no metric claims are named in a warning."],[2615,"A case with zero configured checks — or one where every check is `required = false` — scores\n`1.0` under all three metrics (vacuously). This is the same \"no signal without `checks`\" gap\ndescribed in Setup."],[3232,"A catalog lets you discover skills and add them by their canonical IDs. Each\nrepository is an entry in `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` in `skill-project.toml`.\nLower priority numbers are searched first. Explicit `--repository NAME` selection\navoids ambiguity when several catalogs offer the same ID."],[3347,"A composed Manifest's `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` join the consuming project's for\nresolution, so a shared `repository` origin finds the catalog its own Manifest names. A local\nrepository `path` is relative to the Manifest that declares it. When two Manifests define the same\nrepository name differently, installation stops and asks you to rename one; identical definitions\nare merged. `fastskill repo` commands list and edit only the project's own repositories."],[3355,"A content digest names the exact files of a skill directory and is written as\n`sha256-tree-v2:<hex>`. A lockfile from an earlier release may hold 64-character digests\nwithout that prefix; they are still verified, with a warning, and are replaced when fastskill\nnext rewrites that entry. fastskill releases before this format report a checksum mismatch on\nthe new form, so upgrade every machine and CI job that shares the lockfile."],[2676,"A CSV file of eval cases with `id`, `prompt`, and `should_trigger` columns"],[3217,"A digest proves that selected content has not changed; it does not establish that\nthe instructions or scripts are safe. Review sources before making them available\nto agents. See the security model."],[3210,"A Git marketplace, local catalog, HTTP registry, or ZIP catalog"],[3208,"A Git origin with a branch or tag"],[3359,"A global FastSkill directory is not automatically an agent's discovery directory.\nConfirm the location your agent reads or access global skills through MCP.\nGlobal lock restoration does not require a project manifest."],[3387,"A group filter excluded the owning root."],[568,"A judge is one native chat completion per trial — no agent, no tools, nothing injected that the judge's author did not write. Each exchange is recorded in full in `trial-N/judgments.json`, and the engine, never the model, computes every score from the reply."],[1318,"A legacy value remains: under `--check`, or an entry left as is, or a legacy bundle artifact"],[1309,"A legacy value whose content is not installed, or whose installed content no longer matches it, is\nleft as it is and reported with the reason. Run `fastskill project install` to restore the content,\nthen run `project repin` again."],[3206,"A local dependency, optionally editable"],[619,"A number whose provenance is gone cannot be compared with last month's, so the scorecard records four identities beside the metrics:"],[1321,"A project without `skills.lock` has nothing to re-pin and exits `0`."],[3341,"A project's `skill-project.toml` defines the installation directory and desired\nskills. FastSkill finds it by walking up from your working directory. Paths in the\nmanifest are relative to the manifest directory, not the calling shell's directory."],[3214,"A project's manifest defines its repository configuration. Give each catalog a\nunique n